From 503316c39d410131355a60a3e8e957cd2ae2206f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 01:18:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/63] libroot: uname() reports RenkuOS as the system name

uname -s, and the sysname field of struct utsname, still said "Haiku".
Report the name of the system that is actually running.

Software that tells systems apart by this name (config.guess, CMake's
CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME, Python's platform module, build scripts that test
`uname -s`) will no longer recognise the system as Haiku; such checks
need to accept RenkuOS too, or this name may be better kept for
compatibility. Raising it here for discussion.

Signed-off-by: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
---
 src/system/libroot/posix/sys/uname.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/system/libroot/posix/sys/uname.c b/src/system/libroot/posix/sys/uname.c
index 1dd0decf6f..352bec8ff9 100644
--- a/src/system/libroot/posix/sys/uname.c
+++ b/src/system/libroot/posix/sys/uname.c
@@ -36,7 +36,7 @@ uname(struct utsname *info)
 
 	get_system_info(&systemInfo);
 
-	strlcpy(info->sysname, "Haiku", sizeof(info->sysname));
+	strlcpy(info->sysname, "RenkuOS", sizeof(info->sysname));
 
 	haikuRevision = __get_haiku_revision();
 	if (haikuRevision[0] != '\0')
-- 
